      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a case of a 65-year old man diagnosed with retinal vasoproliferative tumour secondary to posterior uveitis. The fluorescein angiography shows an interesting meteor-like leak emanating from the tumour and rising towards the superior retina in the later frames of the angiogram. Pictorially, we call it the \"Retinal Meteor\" and also describe the possible mechanism for this pattern of leakage."},
